{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lit Query is written in TypeScript and reuses TanStack Query Core's type system. The most important rule is the same as every other adapter: give your query and mutation functions well-defined return types, and the result accessors will infer from them."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"query-inference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Inference"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { LitElement } from 'lit'\nimport { createQueryController } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\ntype Todo = {\n  id: number\n  title: string\n}\n\nasync function fetchTodos(): Promise<Todo[]> {\n  const response = await fetch('/api/todos')\n  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch todos')\n  return response.json() as Promise<Todo[]>\n}\n\nclass TodosView extends LitElement {\n  private readonly todos = createQueryController(this, {\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: fetchTodos,\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    const query = this.todos()\n    // query.data is Todo[] | undefined until success is known.\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Checking "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isSuccess"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPending"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isError"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" narrows the result just like TanStack Query Core result types:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const query = this.todos()\n\nif (query.isSuccess) {\n  query.data\n  // Todo[]\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"mutation-inference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutation Inference"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { LitElement } from 'lit'\nimport { createMutationController } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\ntype CreateTodoInput = {\n  title: string\n}\n\ntype Todo = {\n  id: number\n  title: string\n}\n\nasync function addTodo(input: CreateTodoInput): Promise<Todo> {\n  const response = await fetch('/api/todos', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    body: JSON.stringify(input),\n  })\n  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Failed to create todo')\n  return response.json() as Promise<Todo>\n}\n\nclass AddTodoButton extends LitElement {\n  private readonly mutation = createMutationController(this, {\n    mutationFn: addTodo,\n  })\n\n  private add() {\n    this.mutation.mutate({ title: 'Learn Lit Query' })\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"extracting-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extracting Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"link","href":"./reference/functions/queryOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"./reference/functions/infiniteQueryOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"infiniteQueryOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"link","href":"./reference/functions/mutationOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutationOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" when you want to share typed options between controllers and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" calls."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { LitElement } from 'lit'\nimport {\n  QueryClient,\n  createQueryController,\n  noop,\n  queryOptions,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nfunction todosOptions() {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: fetchTodos,\n    staleTime: 5_000,\n  })\n}\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nclass TodosView extends LitElement {\n  private readonly todos = createQueryController(this, todosOptions())\n}\n\nvoid queryClient.query(todosOptions()).catch(noop)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The branded "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" returned from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" also helps APIs like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryClient.getQueryData"},{"type":"text","value":" understand the data type."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"global-register-types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Global Register Types"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Because "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/lit-query"},{"type":"text","value":" re-exports TanStack Query Core, module augmentation is written against "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/lit-query"},{"type":"text","value":" in Lit apps:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\ntype AppQueryKey = ['todos' | 'projects', ...ReadonlyArray<unknown>]\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/lit-query' {\n  interface Register {\n    queryKey: AppQueryKey\n    mutationKey: AppQueryKey\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the generated reference for Lit-specific "},{"type":"link","href":"./reference/index.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"option and result types"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"query-inference","text":"Query Inference","level":2},{"id":"mutation-inference","text":"Mutation Inference","level":2},{"id":"extracting-options","text":"Extracting Options","level":2},{"id":"global-register-types","text":"Global Register Types","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nLit Query is written in TypeScript and reuses TanStack Query Core's type system. The most important rule is the same as every other adapter: give your query and mutation functions well-defined return types, and the result accessors will infer from them.\n\n## Query Inference\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement } from 'lit'\nimport { createQueryController } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\ntype Todo = {\n  id: number\n  title: string\n}\n\nasync function fetchTodos(): Promise<Todo[]> {\n  const response = await fetch('/api/todos')\n  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch todos')\n  return response.json() as Promise<Todo[]>\n}\n\nclass TodosView extends LitElement {\n  private readonly todos = createQueryController(this, {\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: fetchTodos,\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    const query = this.todos()\n    // query.data is Todo[] | undefined until success is known.\n  }\n}\n```\n\nChecking `isSuccess`, `isPending`, `isError`, or `status` narrows the result just like TanStack Query Core result types:\n\n```ts\nconst query = this.todos()\n\nif (query.isSuccess) {\n  query.data\n  // Todo[]\n}\n```\n\n## Mutation Inference\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement } from 'lit'\nimport { createMutationController } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\ntype CreateTodoInput = {\n  title: string\n}\n\ntype Todo = {\n  id: number\n  title: string\n}\n\nasync function addTodo(input: CreateTodoInput): Promise<Todo> {\n  const response = await fetch('/api/todos', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    body: JSON.stringify(input),\n  })\n  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Failed to create todo')\n  return response.json() as Promise<Todo>\n}\n\nclass AddTodoButton extends LitElement {\n  private readonly mutation = createMutationController(this, {\n    mutationFn: addTodo,\n  })\n\n  private add() {\n    this.mutation.mutate({ title: 'Learn Lit Query' })\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Extracting Options\n\nUse [`queryOptions`](./reference/functions/queryOptions.md), [`infiniteQueryOptions`](./reference/functions/infiniteQueryOptions.md), and [`mutationOptions`](./reference/functions/mutationOptions.md) when you want to share typed options between controllers and `QueryClient` calls.\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement } from 'lit'\nimport {\n  QueryClient,\n  createQueryController,\n  noop,\n  queryOptions,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nfunction todosOptions() {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: fetchTodos,\n    staleTime: 5_000,\n  })\n}\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nclass TodosView extends LitElement {\n  private readonly todos = createQueryController(this, todosOptions())\n}\n\nvoid queryClient.query(todosOptions()).catch(noop)\n```\n\nThe branded `queryKey` returned from `queryOptions` also helps APIs like `queryClient.getQueryData` understand the data type.\n\n## Global Register Types\n\nBecause `@tanstack/lit-query` re-exports TanStack Query Core, module augmentation is written against `@tanstack/lit-query` in Lit apps:\n\n```ts\nimport '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\ntype AppQueryKey = ['todos' | 'projects', ...ReadonlyArray<unknown>]\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/lit-query' {\n  interface Register {\n    queryKey: AppQueryKey\n    mutationKey: AppQueryKey\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee the generated reference for Lit-specific [option and result types](./reference/index.md).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: typescript\ntitle: TypeScript\n---\n\nLit Query is written in TypeScript and reuses TanStack Query Core's type system. The most important rule is the same as every other adapter: give your query and mutation functions well-defined return types, and the result accessors will infer from them.\n\n## Query Inference\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement } from 'lit'\nimport { createQueryController } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\ntype Todo = {\n  id: number\n  title: string\n}\n\nasync function fetchTodos(): Promise<Todo[]> {\n  const response = await fetch('/api/todos')\n  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch todos')\n  return response.json() as Promise<Todo[]>\n}\n\nclass TodosView extends LitElement {\n  private readonly todos = createQueryController(this, {\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: fetchTodos,\n  })\n\n  render() {\n    const query = this.todos()\n    // query.data is Todo[] | undefined until success is known.\n  }\n}\n```\n\nChecking `isSuccess`, `isPending`, `isError`, or `status` narrows the result just like TanStack Query Core result types:\n\n```ts\nconst query = this.todos()\n\nif (query.isSuccess) {\n  query.data\n  // Todo[]\n}\n```\n\n## Mutation Inference\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement } from 'lit'\nimport { createMutationController } from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\ntype CreateTodoInput = {\n  title: string\n}\n\ntype Todo = {\n  id: number\n  title: string\n}\n\nasync function addTodo(input: CreateTodoInput): Promise<Todo> {\n  const response = await fetch('/api/todos', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    body: JSON.stringify(input),\n  })\n  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Failed to create todo')\n  return response.json() as Promise<Todo>\n}\n\nclass AddTodoButton extends LitElement {\n  private readonly mutation = createMutationController(this, {\n    mutationFn: addTodo,\n  })\n\n  private add() {\n    this.mutation.mutate({ title: 'Learn Lit Query' })\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Extracting Options\n\nUse [`queryOptions`](./reference/functions/queryOptions.md), [`infiniteQueryOptions`](./reference/functions/infiniteQueryOptions.md), and [`mutationOptions`](./reference/functions/mutationOptions.md) when you want to share typed options between controllers and `QueryClient` calls.\n\n```ts\nimport { LitElement } from 'lit'\nimport {\n  QueryClient,\n  createQueryController,\n  noop,\n  queryOptions,\n} from '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\nfunction todosOptions() {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: fetchTodos,\n    staleTime: 5_000,\n  })\n}\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\n\nclass TodosView extends LitElement {\n  private readonly todos = createQueryController(this, todosOptions())\n}\n\nvoid queryClient.query(todosOptions()).catch(noop)\n```\n\nThe branded `queryKey` returned from `queryOptions` also helps APIs like `queryClient.getQueryData` understand the data type.\n\n## Global Register Types\n\nBecause `@tanstack/lit-query` re-exports TanStack Query Core, module augmentation is written against `@tanstack/lit-query` in Lit apps:\n\n```ts\nimport '@tanstack/lit-query'\n\ntype AppQueryKey = ['todos' | 'projects', ...ReadonlyArray<unknown>]\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/lit-query' {\n  interface Register {\n    queryKey: AppQueryKey\n    mutationKey: AppQueryKey\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee the generated reference for Lit-specific [option and result types](./reference/index.md).\n"}
